Member Signature Effect <code>config</code> object The resolved configuration. <code>refresh</code> <code>refresh(root = document)</code> → <code>this</code> Scan <code>root</code> for matching links and attach to new ones. <code>add</code> <code>add(target)</code> → <code>this</code> Attach to one <code>Element</code> or an array-like list of elements, without a scan. <code>show</code> <code>show(link)</code> → <code>Promise&lt;void&gt; \| undefined</code> Fetch and show the preview for <code>link</code>, bypassing hover intent. Returns <code>undefined</code> when the link has no usable <code>href</code>. <code>hide</code> <code>hide()</code> → <code>this</code> Hide the card now. Does not call <code>onHide</code>. <code>destroy</code> <code>destroy()</code> → <code>void</code> Cancel timers, remove the <code>window</code> scroll and resize listeners, and remove the popup element. <pre><code>const inst = hrefc();

inst.refresh();                                  // after inserting links
inst.add(document.querySelector('#late-link'));
await inst.show(myLink);                         // manual trigger
inst.hide();
inst.destroy();
</code></pre> <p><code>refresh</code>, <code>add</code> and <code>hide</code> return the instance, so calls can be chained.</p> <p>Note</p> <p><code>destroy()</code> forgets which links were attached but does not remove the listeners already on those links. Do not reuse a destroyed instance; create a new one.</p>

Hook Signature Called when <code>onShow</code> <code>(data, link, popupEl) =&gt; void</code> A card is shown. <code>onHide</code> <code>(link) =&gt; void</code> The card hides after the pointer leaves. <code>onError</code> <code>(error, link) =&gt; void</code> Fetching or extraction failed. <pre><code>hrefc({
  onShow: (data, link, popupEl) =&gt; console.log('shown', data.url),
  onHide: (link) =&gt; console.log('hidden'),
  onError: (err, link) =&gt; console.warn(err),
});
</code></pre> <p>Exceptions thrown in hooks are caught and ignored.</p>
